			"SHA": "09782fa20a60cc3f43081b7b9741c1d99e2f3b38"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-26T17:15:00Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1959,
				2
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Wind): Align Tauri invoke command names to snake_case convention\n\nThe Tauri commands `VineSubscribeNotifications` and `VineSubscriberCount` are registered on the Rust (Mountain) backend where the standard naming convention is snake_case. Wind's `tauri.invoke` and `Module.invoke` callers were using PascalCase, which would fail at runtime since the Tauri IPC dispatcher matches command names case-sensitively against the backend registration.\n\nRename both invoke targets in `Source/Effect/Vine/NotificationStream.ts` to match the Rust-side registrations: `vine_subscribe_notifications` and `vine_subscriber_count`. The error message strings are updated to match for consistency.\n\nNo behavioral changes — the commands themselves and their payload schemas are identical.",
			"SHA": "ec67e70c68f4b5e783af35224cb7945b4a09d16e"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-26T15:41:40Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1959,
				1
			],
			"Message": "chore(Wind): Remove unused ModelUpdateContent IPC channel route\n\nThe `model:updateContent` IPC route defined in Channel.ts is no longer consumed by any active IPC caller. The Model subsystem now handles content updates through a different path — likely via the per-subsystem tier routing or direct content synchronization effects rather than a named channel dispatch.\n\nRemove the route constant and its `// --- Model ---` section header from the channel catalog to keep the route registry clean and avoid confusion during debugging.",
			"SHA": "f2f0d2b1b79b88f2092d53d64a398b5dd40ad2cc"
		}
	],
